---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="Report a vulnerability"
  description="How to report a security issue in SecuritySolution.tech websites and systems, and what you can expect from us."
>
  <article class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h1>Report a vulnerability</h1>
      <p class="lead">If you find a security issue in one of our websites or systems, we want to hear about it.</p>

      <h2>How to report</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${site.securityEmail}`}>{site.securityEmail}</a> with a description of the issue, the steps
        to reproduce it, and the impact you expect. Screenshots or a short proof of concept help us move faster.
      </p>

      <h2>What you can expect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We acknowledge your report within 3 business days.</li>
        <li>We keep you updated while we investigate and fix the issue.</li>
        <li>Once it is resolved, we credit you publicly if you would like that.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Scope</h2>
      <p>{site.name} and its subdomains.</p>

      <h2>Please do not</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Access, change or delete data that is not yours.</li>
        <li>Run denial-of-service tests or high-volume automated scans.</li>
        <li>Use social engineering, phishing or physical attacks.</li>
        <li>Share the issue publicly before we have fixed it.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Safe harbour</h2>
      <p>
        We will not take legal action against security research that follows this policy in good faith. We do not run a
        paid bug bounty at the moment.
      </p>

      <p>
        Machine-readable contact details are published in our
        <a href="/.well-known/security.txt">security.txt</a> file.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
